  "details": "Hello, I was just brainstorming about the new stickers feature that was announced. If I'm hosting an instance, whether it's Friends+ or Group Public, I understand there will be an option to locally hide the sticker or report it.\n\nI thought of a scenario where it would be possible for an instance moderator to either click on a user to prevent them from laying down stickers in the instance, or by clicking on a sticker and hiding it for everyone (and subsequently hiding it if it's placed down again; probably a temporary sticker/emoji ID blacklist, in the API).\n\nI hope this becomes possible during development. Please and thank you!",
